// Dialog :
"P3645585252" "You found a series of documents relating to someone named Detective Martins."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2043841890" "You have fended off the Praetorian Clockwork and saved the life of No Mind!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3561473610" "No Mind, huh? Never heard of him, but it sounds like you did right by him. It's good to see you've got some leadership skills, kiddo. I can't guarantee I'll be around forever, so I... well, let's just say it's good to see you taking charge when you need to. Anyway, what did you find?<br><br><color orange>You explain to Twinshot what you've found.</color><br><br>Hmm... well, it's not much, but it's something. I think this calls for a good old-fashioned investigation!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Serge 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P32864716" "Oh, no no no no NO! That look, it's so... ancient. I haven't seen designs like that in years!"
// Answer Text :
"P3300821713" "...Excuse me?"
// Page ExcuseMe Text :
"P3724452791" "Your look! Your appearance! Your visual impact! It's all wrong, it just won't do! Come, I have the perfect belt that would just..."
// Answer Text :
"P4277138997" "*Ahem* That's not why I'm here."
// Page NotWhyHere Text :
"P4141597222" "No, darling, that's why <b>I'm</b> here. Heroes, gods, and champions all come to ME to make sure they strike the right tone with their appearance. And right now, the tone I'm getting from you is 'wobbly'. You don't want to pounce on a gang of Outcasts only for them to laugh at your wobbly costume, do you?<br><br>Let me take you to one of our rooms, I have some things that would make you look absolutely fantastic. The press won't be able to keep their cameras off of you."
// Answer Text :
"P2629249376" "Wobbly? LOOK, I'm here to... ARGH!"
// Page Frustrated Text :
"P3234282841" "Whoa, calm down, darling. What's the matter?<br><br><color orange>You show Serge the box of old costume parts, and explain where you found them.</color><br><br>Oh, THOSE old things? Oh, darling, you're sweet, but I don't need those anymore. Those are some old doo-dads from when I moved out of my studio in L.A. I decided I didn't need them anymore, so I just... left them behind. It's sad, but in the fashion industry you must always be looking <i>forward</i>, or you'll only end up stale."
// Answer Text :
"P3317073670" "That still doesn't explain why it ended up in a warehouse filled with Clockwork!"
// Page Clockwork Text :
"P3433893200" "Warehouse... on 15th and Maple, yes? I used to lease that place for storage, but that was <i>years</i> ago. I haven't the foggiest idea what it's being used for now."
// Answer Text :
"P1211560443" "*sigh* Alright. Thanks for your help."
// Page Thanks Text :
"P522910949" "Anytime, darling. Anytime."
// Answer Text :
"P2787317035" "Whatever."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Detective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3820382907" "Yo. How ya doing... do I know you?"
// Answer Text :
"P4285863530" "Doing just fine, Detective Martins. Mind taking a look at these?"
// Page TakeALook Text :
"P1512706569" "Taking a look at wha...<br><br><color orange>Detective Martins turns pale as you show him the receipts you found.</color><br><br>I, uh, I don't know what those are. Dunno why you'd come lookin' fer me anyway..."
// Answer Text :
"P2063323408" "These receipts have your name on them, Martins. What are all these gadgets for?"
// Page Gadgets Text :
"P3988930282" "<color orange>Detective Martins pulls you aside and begins speaking in a hushed whisper.</color><br><br>Alright, alright. You got me. I don't know how you found those, but it doesn't matter anymore. Just... just don't tell the FBSA, ok? My boss is ready to string me up as it is, I don't need to give him any ammo."
// Answer Text :
"P300742022" "Uh... don't tell them what?"
// Page TellHim Text :
"P386813383" "<color orange>Detective Martins looks at you quizzically.</color><br><br>Well... that I'm the Shadow Commando."
// Answer Text :
"P1300659197" "Wait, the Shadow who what now?"
// Page ShadowWhat Text :
"P3920838685" "SHH! For the love of my precarious career, <i>please</i> keep your voice down.<br><br>Some nights I do a little moonlight hero work as the Shadow Commando. Problem is, it's unlicensed, and the FBSA doesn't take kindly to unlicensed heroes."
// Answer Text :
"P3062868721" "Why don't you just get a license, then?"
// Page License Text :
"P4073777531" "Can't, it's against regulations. Conflict of interest. It's my job to stay in touch with Heroes and make sure they keep on top of any reported crimes here in Steel Canyon.<br><br>If I do that, and I'm also a registered Hero, well, then some people start to complain. They start saying that I only give the flashy, front-page jobs - like stopping bank heists - to Hero pals of mine, instead of doing my job fair-and-square. It's a bunch of hogwash if you ask me, but those are the rules."
// Answer Text :
"P875841416" "So... this has nothing to do with the Clockwork?"
// Page Clockwork Text :
"P166205495" "Don't know what you mean, kid. I'm just a guy with a bit of a double life, that's all."
// Answer Text :
"P272720246" "Alright, Martins. I'll leave you be."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Store 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P497858877" "Hi! Welcome to Cooke's Electronics. My name is Sonia, how can I help you today?"
// Answer Text :
"P2119915916" "Hi, Sonia. I'm looking for a High Frequency Signal Transmitter."
// Page Transmitter Text :
"P1852301974" "Then you've come to the right place! What frequency range were you looking for? Or would you rather take a look at our selection?"
// Answer Text :
"P1121618375" "Do you have anything that could broadcast signals across multiple dimensions?"
// Page Dimensions Text :
"P289123257" "<color orange>On the word 'dimensions', Sonia immediately breaks into a nervous smile.</color><br><br>Uhhh, I'm... sorry, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}, we don't stock that kind of thing here. Selling interdimensional tech is actually regulated by D.A.T.A. and you'd need a special permit to-"
// Answer Text :
"P3146939913" "That's funny. This tag right here says you've sold one before."
// Page SoldBefore Text :
"P2249999347" "<color orange>Beads of sweat begin to appear on Sonia's forehead</color><br><br>Oh, uh, I'm sorry, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}, you must be mistaken! We would be happy to help you with any other product that you see here, and-"
// Answer Text :
"P3693597319" "Sonia. Please. I'm not stupid."
// Page NotStupid Text :
"P2206434965" "Alright, alright! I... I may have sold someone an Interdimensional Signal Relay a couple weeks ago. I'm sorry! I know it's against regulations, but he paid good money and I figured it could only end up helping people anyway, so I..."
// Answer Text :
"P4015764995" "Who did you sell it to?"
// Page SoldTo Text :
"P1435565883" "I'm sorry, I... I never got his name."
// Answer Text :
"P914208518" "You sold illegal hardware to someone without even getting their ID?!?"
// Page NoName Text :
"P2483089809" "<color orange>Sonia glares at you.</color><br><br>Look, do you know how many Heroes walk through that door every day? They're all Cyber-this, Techno-that, and they all look the same. Fancy, high-tech gizmos and helmets that hide their faces. You expect me to ID every single cape that walks in here?<br><br>I mean, come on. You must know the drill by now. Even if you don't shop here, you probably go to Pandora's Box or something. They've gotta be the same way."
// Answer Text :
"P1721364468" "Why would I do that?"
// Page WhyShop Text :
"P3603755811" "<color orange>Sonia rolls her eyes at you.</color><br><br>For Enhancements, duh! Why does any hero ever walk through that door? You all strut in here, talking about power output and damage resistance percentages, as if I'd care if you got your face smashed in by some Troll.<br><br>I don't get paid enough to deal with you people!"
// Answer Text :
"P2089047852" "Whoa, okay. I think I'm done here. Don't leave town, Sonia."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2335169855" "Those items you found in the warehouse may not lead anywhere, but anything related to the Praetorians' presence here is worth looking into.<br><br>You're going to need to take care of this one yourself, kiddo. Proton's tied up with lab work, and he's managed to rope Dillo into retrieving parts for some temporal doohickey he's been working on. I asked Grym to give Flambeaux a crash course in tactical combat, and I'm willing to bet that teaching that hothead -anything- is going to take a while. As for me... well, I've got to talk to a few people, work some stuff out."
// AcceptString :
"P2769032346" "Is everything ok?"
// SendOffString :
"P1117489689" "<color orange>Twinshot sighs.</color><br><br>My past is catching up with me, kiddo. I've got a lot of baggage that I thought I'd left at the station, but it doesn't want to stay put, you know? I'll be fine, don't you worry about me. I just have some loose ends to tie up, before...<br><br><color orange>Twinshot trails off, losing herself in thought.</color><br><br>Er, anyway. Look into the stuff you found at that warehouse, and see if there are any connections to the Clockwork that were swarming the place. If you turn anything up, let me know."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P750034756" "<color deepskyblue>Unusual Suspects</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1604394659" "Investigate the Box of Costume Parts"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2192677464" "Costume parts, huh? That sounds like Icon's gig. You may want to hop over there and ask around."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3103888318" "Serge offered to give you a makeover, but he didn't have any useful info for you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2707579679" "Investigate the Gadget Receipts"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3150330044" "Those receipts do seem mighty fishy, especially for someone on a Detective's salary. Definitely worth checking out."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3835648037" "You learned a little too much about Detective Martins's night life, but still no leads."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P513581026" "Investigate the Transmitter Tag"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2180535762" "You said that transmitter was still running when you found it, right? This just might be our lead. Go get 'em, kiddo!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3601489382" "You discovered that a Cooke's Electronics employee sold illegal contraband to an unknown hero. This just might lead somewhere!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1442299970" "So. Someone went all Black Market on us, eh? Well, it's something, that's for sure. Anyone with an interest in sending messages across dimensions is probably tied in with the Praetorians somehow.<br><br>Give me a moment to mull all this over. This is something we're going to want to look into, for sure. I just want to make sure we do it right."
// RandomFameString :
"P1680851863" "{HeroName} must be really serious about {Hero.gender=male his|her} Enhancements. I saw {Hero.gender=male him|her} over at Cooke's giving an employee the third degree!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Computer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3726501763" "<color skyblue>ACCESSING.........<br><br>IDENTITY CONFIRMED: {HeroName}<br>ACCESS GRANTED"
// Answer Text :
"P2014559239" "[Search the database for any activity regarding the High Frequency Signal Transmitter]"
// Page Transmitter Text :
"P3784037866" "<color orange>A long list of dates, times, and locations scrolls onto the screen. Most of these related directly to D.A.T.A., S.E.R.A.P.H., and Portal Corp.<br><br>You don't find anything unusual until you stumble onto one entry:</color><br><br><color skyblue>ENTRY DELETED</color><br><br><color orange>The time of deletion appears to be just minutes before your search."
// Answer Text :
"P1417609936" "Damn! [Trace the database deletion request]"
// Page Deletion Text :
"P1900834247" "<color skyblue>DATABASE DELETION REQUEST TRACED TO IP ADDRESS:<br>3015:db6:97c4:9e1:2420:9b3f:073:8347<br><br>LOCATION: <color red>SHINING STARS HQ"
// Answer Text :
"P1542464271" "What? But who would have-"
// Page WhoDeleted Text :
"P3364454791" "<color orange>You notice a flashing item at the bottom corner of the screen:</color><br><br><color red>CRITICAL FILE:</color> <color skyblue>SHINING STARS MEMBER PROFILES AND RISK ASSESSMENT"
// Answer Text :
"P1938636107" "Hmm... [Open the file]"
// Page StarsProfile Text :
"P331266337" "<color orange>The file contains six separate entries, one for each member of the team. Most of them just contain basic info on your team, with members marked as "Low-risk".<br><br>Two of them are marked as <color red>Important</color> - Flambeaux and Twinshot."
// Answer Text :
"P3018067361" "[Open Flambeaux's entry]"
// Page Flambeaux Text :
"P313345501" "<color skyblue>CODENAME: Flambeaux<br>FULL NAME: *******  *******<br><br>PSYCHOLOGICAL PROFILE:<br>Flambeaux exhibits classic signs of <color red>Narcissistic Personality Disorder<color skyblue>, which could raise the possibility of unsanctioned violent behavior.<br><br>There is a high probability that if Flambeaux does not achieve the fame and attention that she seeks in her role as a Hero, she may turn to more drastic methods.<br><br>RECOMMENDATION:<br>Monitor Flambeaux's progress and maturation as a Hero, and make preparations for the possibility that Flambeaux turns to <color red>Vigilantism<color skyblue> or <color red>Villainy<color skyblue> in order to gain fame or respect."
// Answer Text :
"P2818447944" "Well, that does sound like Flambeaux... [Open Twinshot's entry]"
// Page Twinshot Text :
"P2863221316" "<color skyblue>CODENAME: Twinshot<br>FULL NAME: Unknown<br><br>KNOWN ASSOCIATES: Maelstrom <color red>(Praetorian)<color skyblue><br><br>BACKGROUND:<br>Little information on Twinshot's past exists, but it is likely that she is a surviving member of the now-defunct military ops team 'Ultimatum'. Her combat training and connection with the rogue soldier 'Maelstrom' reinforce this assessment.<br><br><color red>WARNING:<color skyblue> Maelstrom's reappearance in Primal Earth suggests that Twinshot has remained in contact with him. It is highly likely that Twinshot is working from within the Shining Stars as an agent of Praetoria.<br><br>RECOMMENDATION:<br>Twinshot represents both a danger to Primal Earth and a significant flight risk. Keep under surveillance and proceed with extreme caution."
// Answer Text :
"P3634638581" "Oh, Twinshot..."
// Page Alert Text :
"P2517439857" "<color orange>Just as you're about to close down the terminal, alarms begin blaring in the Phalanx council room. The screen on the terminal goes blank, then begins to flash text on the screen:<br><br><color red>WARNING.....WARNING.....WARNING<br><br><color skyblue>MULTIPLE TEMPORAL ANOMALIES DETECTED IN THE NEAR VICINITY<br><br>THERE IS A 97% PROBABILITY THAT INTRUDERS HAVE INFILTRATED THE MANSION</color><br><br>WARNING.....WARNING.....WARNING"
// Answer Text :
"P1129898879" "What the-"
// Page Attack Text :
"P518357535" "<color orange>You hear the sound of whirring motors behind you!"
// Answer Text :
"P1114523752" "[Defend yourself!]"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Grym 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3207671806" "{HeroName}. The trail of your aura shimmers with pain and rage. What is the matter?"
// Answer Text :
"P3146840620" "I think Twinshot just tried to kill me, Grym."
// Page KillMe Text :
"P1587160353" "<color orange>Grym's eyes widen, and he wrinkles his nose at you.</color><br><br>That is a bold accusation, {HeroName}. Are you confident in this claim?<br><br><color orange>You explain to Grym what you found using Manticore's database, and how the Clockwork ambushed you shortly afterwards.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3647191615" "It's hard to come to any other conclusion, Grym."
// Page Conclusion Text :
"P2876882929" "<color orange>Grym growls under his breath.</color><br><br>Sadly, I believe you are correct. This betrayal does not surprise me, {HeroName}. Our comrade Twinshot has wavered as of late. She suffers under the weight of past deeds. I had <i>hoped</i> she was strong enough to carry them.<br><br><color orange>Grym's snout curls into a snarl, baring his teeth.</color><br><br>Apparently, I was mistaken."
// Answer Text :
"P909700058" "So what do we do now?"
// Page DoNow Text :
"P1925289838" "We will confront Twinshot when the time is right. Return to her, and reveal to her nothing. If she realizes that we suspect her, she may attempt to accelerate her plans, or even to flee.<br><br>When we strike, we must ensure that she is unaware until it is too late to escape."
// Answer Text :
"P3383947254" "Alright... I guess it's the only way. I'll be back soon, Grym."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P84180314" "Alright, kiddo. I just had a little confab with Proton, and we both agree that this illicit merchandise deal may be our lead.<br><br>Proton suggested that I use Manticore's database to crosscheck the info we got from the gal at Cooke's. I want to let you get first crack at it, though, since you did the legwork on this one.<br><br>You up for a trip back to the mansion?"
// AcceptString :
"P1397612060" "Sure thing, Twinshot."
// SendOffString :
"P1420254084" "Awesome. I already got the go-ahead from our benefactor to use his chateau in our investigation. He's working on some Phalanx stuff at the moment, so you'll have the place to yourself.<br><br>I feel like we're getting close to this, kiddo. Have at it."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P4078891044" "<color deepskyblue>When A Praetorian Calls</color>"

